  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member using the modern composer, I want the « Répondre » overlay strip above the card removed, keeping only its buttons and making them a little more visible, so that the composer takes less room over the page.\n\n### Wanted (operator, 2026-11-16, iPhone, Réglages › Expérimental › « Composer moderne » on)\n\n- **Remove the overlay space** above the composer card that holds the title « Répondre » (also « Modifier » and the MP titles, if they share the same strip).\n- **Keep the buttons** above the composer: **Fermer** and **Brouillons** on the left, **Envoyer** on the right.\n- **Adjust their colour so they are slightly more visible** over the page: today they fade into the content behind. Use a stronger glyph tint and a subtle glass or capsule background; send keeps the accent. Contrast is checked against light and dark pages.\n- The hit areas stay at 44 pt or more. The 8 pt shared gap (`FloatingSpacing.gap`, #895) is kept between the buttons and the card.\n\n### Where\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/ModernComposer/` (`ComposerChrome.swift`, `ModernComposer.swift`), behind `EXPERIMENTAL(modernComposer, #904)`. The default composer (option off) is unchanged.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No title strip; the three buttons sit directly above the card, Fermer and Brouillons on the left and Envoyer on the right.\n- [ ] The buttons are readable on light and dark pages (a contrast check in a test, as for the theme tokens).\n- [ ] The option off: the composer is unchanged (a test).\n- [ ] Device check in the general review.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
